{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1271694-funny-little-things-you-noticed-in-exalted","id":1271694,"title":"Funny little things you noticed in exalted","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-11-28T22:11:47-08:00","id":1271694,"title":"Funny little things you noticed in exalted","content":"So! Funny little things you see in exalted. Shout outs. Historical references. Little funny jokes. <br /> <br /> So I'll start. <br /> <br /> I was looking at things. Then I realized something. Baseline exalted, without charms, are... comic book badass normals. Think about it. They heal absurdly fast, healing in a month where most people would be crippled. They're way too competent. That is, they don't get a penalty for having zero dots in a skill. They survive blows that should kill other people (more soak and health levels). They get heroic willpower (virtue roll) to do previously impossible feats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T22:48:24-08:00","id":1271700,"title":"","content":"I can read the tvtropes exposure between your lines~.<br /> <br /> Taking an expanded view of Exalted, I appreciated how in one of the novels (Relic of the Dawn, maybe?) Lilith just casually seduces Dace, and also in Keychain of Creation how Marena runs off with Racer, goes out on the town Twin-Faced Hero style looking for love, inspiring jealousy in Secret, enough to get a lecture about being a homewrecker! Like, Lunars might be the ones out in the sticks, but they don't have any kind of country sexual repression going on! If anything, they've got a big-city view of the hookup. The moon has a thousand faces, and each one can find its own love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-29T22:29:03-08:00","id":1271925,"title":"","content":"Abyssals\u2019 \u201cdress like you\u2019re at a funeral or on a metal album cover to not take penalties in the sun\u201d thing will never stop being extremely amusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T06:50:17-08:00","id":1271967,"title":"","content":"2e mass combat was engineered so that a circle of 5 Exalts forms a magnitude 2 unit with enough officer positions for each exalt to be an officer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T07:08:34-08:00","id":1271971,"title":"","content":"Which reminds me. The 2e's combat system was made, so as to incentivize back to back fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T08:55:37-08:00","id":1271988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1271694-funny-little-things-you-noticed-in-exalted?p=1271971#post1271971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 2e's combat system was made, so as to incentivize back to back fighting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having someone at your back isn't enough to invalidate being targeted by an unexpected attack; combat facing isn't tracked, so the fifth attacker is unexpected regardless of whether or not he's literally standing behind you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-30-2018, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-30T10:38:18-08:00","id":1272015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1271694-funny-little-things-you-noticed-in-exalted?p=1271988#post1271988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having someone at your back isn't enough to invalidate being targeted by an unexpected attack; combat facing isn't tracked, so the fifth attacker is unexpected regardless of whether or not he's literally standing behind you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct, but I'm pretty sure there was a hard limit of 5 people at melee range with you. Though it could be wrong, I haven't looked at 2e rules since 3e came out.<br /> <br /> While, 2e was quite famous for its lethality, when you scaled it back to normal people using normal weapons and armour it was generally much less rocket tag. Because of this the bleeding rules simultaneously made to game more realistic and more like an action movie. Realistic, because normal people weren't dying instantly to every sword swing or arrow shot, but actually bleeding out over a course of minutes like in reality. More like and action movie because Exalts can totally ignore the bleeding and thus shrug off the little hits that would doom a mortal to a slow and painful death. This came into focus a bit when shards came out with gun rules. Some complained that it was unrealistic because it was hard to one shot a person with a gun using the stats given. That is until it was pointed out that with the given stats most mortals would quickly bleed out without some kind of medical aid. Exalts of course take bullets like they are starting in a Die Hard movie, as it should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T22:56:50-08:00","id":1272543,"title":"","content":"More Abyssal amusement:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EX3</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Artful Maiming Onslaught (2m, 2i; Supplemental; Instant; Decisive-only, Stackable): If successful, the attack leaves a painful scarring wound that inflicts a cumulative -1 penalty for the rest of the scene. <b>Scars left on players\u2019 characters look cool rather than disfiguring, unless the player desires otherwise</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you ask me the bolded part really encapsulates the kind of game Exalted is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T10:46:59-08:00","id":1272654,"title":"","content":"Whitewall has moveable type.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T19:28:38-08:00","id":1272752,"title":"","content":"Heaven literally uses chocolate coins for money.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T07:35:22-08:00","id":1275508,"title":"","content":"You know what I find most darkly amusing of Demon of the First Circle? <br /> <br /> You can make the argument that 'you're doing it for the demon's own good' because Malfeas is a horrible, hostile, horrendous place where they're at the bottom rung and they're treated as tools. Hey, even if they're being summoned to be slaves here, at least its better than Malfeas, right? <br /> <br /> Just like another of the reasons slavers tried to pretend slavery was virtuous, along with 'civilize the savage' and 'bringing them to modernity'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T07:46:01-08:00","id":1275511,"title":"","content":"That people can try to argue justifying enslaving or otherwise mistreating a people doesn't particularly strike me as &quot;amusing&quot; and more &quot;a depressing facet of reality.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 12-20-2018, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T07:56:58-08:00","id":1275514,"title":"","content":"Perhaps I have a morbid sense of humour?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T12:28:06-08:00","id":1276676,"title":"","content":"Black Ice Shadow sounds like &quot;Black Eye Shadow&quot; when you say it aloud - and he's the emo-est of Sidereals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T12:57:07-08:00","id":1276679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1271694-funny-little-things-you-noticed-in-exalted?p=1276676#post1276676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Ice Shadow sounds like &amp;quot;Black Eye Shadow&amp;quot; when you say it aloud - and he's the emo-est of Sidereals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Several of the Sid sigs from 2e have punny names.<br /> <br /> Crimson Banner Executioner - the guy who cuts the red tape who works in a bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> The Shepherd of the North Star is busy shepherding around the one thing in the heavens that doesn\u2019t move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T13:42:08-08:00","id":1276685,"title":"","content":"May Blossom may blossom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T14:37:56-08:00","id":1276695,"title":"","content":"One that has and continues to amuse me is that First Age people that predominate in older art tended towards being of the same ethnotype as the Atlanteans in the disney movie. Although I loved that movie growing up so I prefer to call it an accidental omage!<br /> <br /> The silliest and most awesome thing was that 2ed bureaucracy charm that made you auto-zap corrupt individuals if they messed with your organization. Not because of the effect but because of the way the zap is described as randomly shooting out of you through walls, vast distances and potentially dimensions to taser a guy that lied about his name wrong on a random census.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T17:27:24-08:00","id":1276711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1271694-funny-little-things-you-noticed-in-exalted?p=1275511#post1275511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That people can try to argue justifying enslaving or otherwise mistreating a people doesn't particularly strike me as &amp;quot;amusing&amp;quot; and more &amp;quot;a depressing facet of reality.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, slavery ends up being one of those moral stepping stones on the way to modern liberalism. Before the innovation of slavery, when your army took someone else's land, you killed anyone who couldn't run away fast enough. The idea of not taking someone's land when you are able to takes a longer time to form, born out of the idea of the equality of human dignity.<br /> <br /> Demons in Hell get a bum deal though. Serve inhuman, uncaring masters in Hell or serve human masters in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T18:01:37-08:00","id":1276714,"title":"","content":"Luna used to have a Ride Specialty <i>for Gaia</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T19:35:13-08:00","id":1276729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1271694-funny-little-things-you-noticed-in-exalted?p=1276714#post1276714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna used to have a Ride Specialty <i>for Gaia</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait. Used to?<br /> <br /> And I thought sol had a ride specialty for Luna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T02:29:16-08:00","id":1276768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1271694-funny-little-things-you-noticed-in-exalted?p=1276714#post1276714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Luna used to have a Ride Specialty <i>for Gaia</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1271694-funny-little-things-you-noticed-in-exalted?p=1276729#post1276729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait. Used to?<br /> <br /> And I thought sol had a ride specialty for Luna.</div> </div> </div> </div>If both are simultaneously true, then I can only see one conclusion.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Eclipse</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T09:23:12-08:00","id":1277021,"title":"","content":"We don't know how much the lore arond Abyssals will change in 3E, but I always found this tidbit about them super amusing. In 2E, Abyssals don't have the Great Curse, the Neverborn revoke it because why have such a terrible flaw in your tools? However, Abyssals can go Solar again and the Curse isn't reinstated! The cherry on top is that the Abyssals were in large part The Ebon Dragon's idea. TED, the one that must betray, and if he has no one else to betray he betrays himself. And his arguably greatest acomplishment since imprisonment, the Abyssal Exalted's existence, can get rid of the Solar's Achilles Heel. If that isn't poetry, I don't know what is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13696-knurlurzhad","name":"Knurlurzhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T13:43:45-08:00","id":1277069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1271694-funny-little-things-you-noticed-in-exalted?p=1276711#post1276711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, slavery ends up being one of those moral stepping stones on the way to modern liberalism. Before the innovation of slavery, when your army took someone else's land, you killed anyone who couldn't run away fast enough. The idea of not taking someone's land when you are able to takes a longer time to form, born out of the idea of the equality of human dignity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want to take this thread on a massive tangent, but slavery predates all written records, and was found in all ancient &quot;civilised&quot; societies. Ancient Egypt, China, Sumer, etc. It comes hand-in-hand with the development of land ownership and agriculture (probably. Not like we have any written records from the beginning of slavery. But those are things that happened about the same time). Before the innovation of slavery... basically, people were hunter-gatherers, so they didn't have armies or own land. I suppose you could argue that one hunter-gatherer tribe might fight another to drive them out of some prime territory? So I guess you could say you're right from a certain point of view? Armies invading and killing everyone is probably a bit misleading in how people imagine it, when it comes to hunter-gatherers though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demons in Hell get a bum deal though. Serve inhuman, uncaring masters in Hell or serve human masters in Creation. </div> </div> </div>We can agree on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 12-27-2018, 04:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0